  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="667198aa-b93e-559b-81e2-4b618ed52eb4" activityNameId="b29faa59-e493-5630-8225-1853b6c8083d" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Scantling, softwood, solid wood, massive, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Scantling, softwood, solid wood, massive, at plant
The thickness of the scantling is 0.071m. The bill of materials is based on data from two scantling producers. Allocation of co-products is either based on physical properties (wood inputs) or economical properties (working materials, production loss). An unweighted average was calculated.;
UUID: 4cdc0e94-7493-3d21-bcfd-3b956abee9d6
Included are the materials used in a massive scantling. Production losses, work materials, packaging materials, energy demand and the transport of the materials are also included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at scantling producers in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: The corresponding dataset for Switzerland was used as basis. The electricity mix, wood inputs and transports were changed to account for production in Europe. Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4cdc0e94-7493-3d21-bcfd-3b956abee9d6.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
